<section id="work-with-me" aria-label="Work with Susan" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t" style="border-color: var(--color-border)">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[680px] px-6 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold mb-7">Work with me</h2>

    <div class="space-y-5 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Alongside Kaleida, I take on a small number of fractional and advisory clients. The main way
        in is <strong>The Technical Sounding Board</strong>: a monthly retainer where founders and
        engineering leaders get a senior technical and leadership partner to think through the hard
        calls with, without a full-time hire.
      </p>
      <p>
        I know what this is worth because I've been on the buying side of it. When Kaleida's data
        model stopped flexing and half the team wanted to swap the database, what changed the shape
        of that decision was bringing in someone from outside the team to look at what we'd built
        and what we actually wanted. I've written that one up:
        <a href="/speaking/adaconf-2025-data-pivot">Changing the engine mid-flight</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also always up for turning good work into a good story. If you've got a hard problem
        worth digging into, let's build a case study together: real work on a real challenge, written
        up and shared on stage and in writing, with your blessing.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Either way, start with a conversation.</strong> Forty-five minutes, no charge, no
        obligation. Tell me what you're wrestling with and I'll tell you honestly whether I'm the
        right person for it. If I'm not, I'll usually know someone who is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3" role="list">
      <a
        href="mailto:hello@susanbrander.com?subject=Fractional%20%2F%20advisory%20enquiry"
        role="listitem"
        class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium text-sm no-underline hover:no-underline transition-colors"
      >
        Start a conversation
      </a>
      <a
        href="mailto:hello@susanbrander.com?subject=Building%20a%20case%20study%20together"
        role="listitem"
        class="btn-secondary inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md font-medium text-sm no-underline hover:no-underline border transition-colors"
      >
        Build a case study together
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .btn-primary {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
  .btn-secondary {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    border-color: var(--color-border);
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
